---
title: Quantity
order: 11
description: A number input with step buttons, for prints.
---
{% from "docs.njk" import example, usage, props %}
{% from "components/quantity-input/quantity-input.njk" import quantityInput %}
<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Component · &lt;quantity-input&gt;</p>
  <h1>Quantity</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">For prints only. Originals are always one, so don't show this for them. Without JS it's a plain number input. JS adds − and +, which are clamped to min and max.</p>
</header>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="use">
  <h2 id="use">Use it</h2>
  {% set code %}{% raw %}{% from "components/quantity-input/quantity-input.njk" import quantityInput %}
{% if not (product | isOriginal) %}{{ quantityInput({ id: "qty", max: 10 }) }}{% endif %}{% endraw %}{% endset %}
  {{ usage(code) }}
  {{ props([
    ["id / name", "string", "Defaults to quantity."],
    ["value, min, max", "number", "Defaults 1, 1, 10."],
    ["label / hideLabel", "string / boolean", "Defaults to “Quantity”. Hide it only where the context makes it obvious, like a cart line."],
    ["disabled", "boolean", ""]
  ]) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="states">
  <h2 id="states">States</h2>
  <div class="docs-examples">
    {% set ex %}{{ quantityInput({ id: "ex-q1" }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("Default (at the minimum, so − is off)", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ quantityInput({ id: "ex-q2", value: 3, max: 3 }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("At the maximum", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ quantityInput({ id: "ex-q3", disabled: true }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("Disabled", ex) }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="a11y">
  <h2 id="a11y">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Keyboard users type in the input or use the arrow keys. The − and + buttons are for pointers and touch, so they're left out of the tab order, which saves two tab stops on every cart line.</li>
    <li>The buttons have labels like “Decrease quantity of Tulip”.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
